review:
while dr kapilla, azziz and marcus were professional, the treatment by the nursing staff is atrocious.  (exception julius patrick and melissa (new to this facility from main.)

when a nurse tells you they are frustrated and hungry and that you will have to wait until they come back for them to help you... there is something wrong.  when they come back and tell you again while the head nurse (the one i charge of the hospital on this day) is in the room and the hn smirks and does nothing... wow.  well she did go get a compress that dr. azziz has requested 2 hours before... 

i wouldn't come back...

arrived 5:30 am for hip replacement surgery. they all moved me through all the stations pronto! surgery was perfect, all medical professionals that i encountered were professional, polite and helpful. i could not have asked for a better experience! some of the super stars were:
dr. marcelli, best orthopedic surgeon; dr. patterson most capable anesthesiologists;
nurse joel, really cared about my post-op pain levels; nurse tom, prep for surgery;
nurses chrissy and leo, who took care of me. there were many more that were great but i forgot their names. 
i would highly recommend this hospital.
